---
import BaseHead from '../../../components/BaseHead.astro';
import InternationalLessonChrome from '../../../components/InternationalLessonChrome.astro';
const base=import.meta.env.BASE_URL.endsWith('/')?import.meta.env.BASE_URL:import.meta.env.BASE_URL+'/';
---
<!doctype html><html lang="en"><head><BaseHead title="Places to Draw · HARUM NOIR" description="Four places for drawing practice: studio, museum, botanical garden and Brazilian archive. Observe, sketch and verify sources." alternates={[{hreflang:'pt-BR',href:base+'colecoes/lugares/'},{hreflang:'en',href:base+'en/collections/places/'},{hreflang:'es',href:base+'es/colecciones/lugares/'}]}/></head><body><InternationalLessonChrome lang="en" ptHref={base+'colecoes/lugares/'} enHref={base+'en/collections/places/'} esHref={base+'es/colecciones/lugares/'}><main class="places">
<header class="hero"><a class="back" href={base+'en/collections/'}>← All visual collections</a><span class="eyebrow">COLLECTION 06 · PLACE · OBSERVATION</span><h1>Places to draw.</h1><p>Every place is built from relationships: light and shadow, artwork and wall, plant and open space, document and context. Treat the editorial images as observation maps. Use institutional collections to research real works and records.</p><a class="button" href="#places">Choose a place ↓</a><figure class="hero-image"><img src={base+'noir/visual-atlas/museum-gallery.webp'} alt="Editorial museum gallery used to study scale, architecture and space." width="1200" height="800" fetchpriority="high"/><figcaption>Editorial study image; it does not depict a specific institution or artwork.</figcaption></figure></header>
<section id="places" class="intro"><div><span class="eyebrow">FOUR DOORS · ONE PRACTICE</span><h2>See relationships before details.</h2></div><p>These images are original editorial teaching art, not collection records. For research, open the institution's own catalogue, read the item record and check its rights information.</p></section>
<div class="grid">
<article class="card"><figure><img src={base+'noir/visual-atlas/atelier-desk.webp'} alt="Editorial studio desk with a sketchbook and tools in side light." width="900" height="650" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><figcaption>Editorial study · not a collection record</figcaption></figure><div><span class="eyebrow">PLACE 01</span><h2>Studio and window</h2><h3>Observation prompt</h3><p>Where does the light come from? Mark the shadow direction and three broad values.</p><h3>8-minute practice</h3><p>Draw three two-minute thumbnails of the same desk from different framings. Compare the open spaces and develop one.</p><a href="https://www.metmuseum.org/art/collection" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Research objects at The Met ↗</a></div></article>
<article class="card"><figure><img src={base+'noir/visual-atlas/museum-gallery.webp'} alt="Editorial gallery scene for studying scale, architecture and visitors." width="900" height="650" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><figcaption>Editorial study · not a collection record</figcaption></figure><div><span class="eyebrow">PLACE 02</span><h2>Museum gallery</h2><h3>Observation prompt</h3><p>How do the artwork, wall and visitor organize the scene?</p><h3>8-minute practice</h3><p>Draw the room rectangle first. Add only three masses: artwork, architecture and person. Finish with one perspective line.</p><a href="https://www.clevelandart.org/art/collection" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Research the Cleveland Museum of Art collection ↗</a></div></article>
<article class="card"><figure><img src={base+'noir/visual-atlas/collections/botanica-iris.webp'} alt="Editorial iris study in graphite and charcoal for observing plant structure." width="900" height="650" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><figcaption>Editorial study · not a collection record</figcaption></figure><div><span class="eyebrow">PLACE 03</span><h2>Botanical garden</h2><h3>Observation prompt</h3><p>Which axis supports the plant? Where do leaves overlap?</p><h3>8-minute practice</h3><p>Choose a real plant. Mark its axis, group the leaves and leave details until last. Compare direction and spacing instead of copying every leaf.</p><a href="https://www.missouribotanicalgarden.org/plantfinder/plantfindersearch.aspx" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Consult the Missouri Botanical Garden Plant Finder ↗</a></div></article>
<article class="card"><figure><img src={base+'noir/visual-atlas/collections/arquivo-bahia.webp'} alt="Editorial composition inspired by Brazilian visual archives; not a historical document." width="900" height="650" loading="lazy" decoding="async"/><figcaption>Editorial study · not a historical document</figcaption></figure><div><span class="eyebrow">PLACE 04</span><h2>Brazilian archive</h2><h3>Observation prompt</h3><p>What visual clues suggest place, period or use without turning a guess into fact?</p><h3>8-minute practice</h3><p>Open an archive item. Read its creator, date, medium and rights. Draw its main shapes, then label what you observed and what remains a hypothesis.</p><a href="https://bndigital.bn.gov.br/" target="_blank" rel="noreferrer">Explore the Brazilian National Library Digital collection ↗</a></div></article>
</div>
<section class="closing"><span class="eyebrow">EIGHT-MINUTE RITUAL</span><h2>From looking to notebook.</h2><ol><li><b>2 min · frame</b><span>Choose one relationship and draw its largest shape.</span></li><li><b>3 min · compare</b><span>Check direction, scale and negative space.</span></li><li><b>2 min · decide</b><span>Change one thing instead of adding detail.</span></li><li><b>1 min · record</b><span>Write what you saw and what you still need to verify.</span></li></ol><a href={base+'en/references/'}>Continue to visual references →</a></section>
</main></InternationalLessonChrome></body></html>
<style>
.places{max-width:1200px;margin:auto;padding:24px clamp(18px,5vw,68px) 80px;color:var(--paper)}.hero{display:grid;grid-template-columns:1fr .9fr;gap:12px 48px;align-items:center;padding:12px 0 34px;border-bottom:1px solid var(--line)}.back{grid-column:1/-1;color:var(--paper-2);font-size:.78rem}.eyebrow{color:var(--gold);font-size:.67rem;font-weight:700;letter-spacing:.14em;text-transform:uppercase}.hero h1{font-size:clamp(3.5rem,8vw,6.4rem);letter-spacing:-.055em;line-height:.9;margin:16px 0}.hero p,.intro p{max-width:62ch;color:var(--paper-2);line-height:1.7}.button{display:inline-block;margin-top:10px;padding:12px 16px;background:var(--gold);color:#111;text-decoration:none;border-radius:4px}.hero-image{grid-column:2;grid-row:2/6;margin:0}.hero-image img,.card img{display:block;width:100%;height:auto;object-fit:cover}.hero-image figcaption,.card figcaption{padding:8px 10px;color:var(--muted);font-size:.68rem;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.intro{display:grid;grid-template-columns:.8fr 1.2fr;gap:30px;padding:48px 0 20px}.intro h2,.closing h2{font-size:clamp(2rem,4vw,3.6rem);line-height:1;margin:10px 0}.grid{display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(2,minmax(0,1fr));gap:16px}.card{overflow:hidden;border:1px solid var(--line);border-radius:8px;background:#111}.card figure{margin:0;background:#171717}.card img{aspect-ratio:1.45}.card>div{padding:18px}.card h2{font-size:1.7rem;margin:9px 0 18px}.card h3{color:var(--gold);font-size:.8rem;margin:16px 0 5px}.card p{color:var(--paper-2);font-size:.88rem;line-height:1.6;margin:0}.card a,.closing>a{display:inline-block;margin-top:16px;color:var(--gold);font-size:.8rem}.closing{margin:46px 0 0;padding:26px;border:1px solid var(--line);background:#111}.closing ol{list-style:none;display:grid;grid-template-columns:repeat(4,1fr);gap:10px;padding:0}.closing li{display:grid;gap:8px;padding:14px;border-top:1px solid var(--line)}.closing li b{color:var(--gold)}.closing li span{color:var(--paper-2);font-size:.8rem;line-height:1.5}@media(max-width:700px){.hero{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:14px}.hero-image{grid-column:auto;grid-row:auto}.intro{grid-template-columns:1fr;gap:6px;padding-top:34px}.grid{grid-template-columns:1fr}.closing ol{grid-template-columns:1fr 1fr}}@media(max-width:420px){.closing ol{grid-template-columns:1fr}}
</style>